> Thanks for the detailed analysis @Chaunceyctx . I'm still sorting through this, do you think that #107065 is involved with this?

@mattcary 
Yes. look at this log content:
```
E1125 10:20:44.902890 3908451 nestedpendingoperations.go:348] Operation for "{volumeName:kubernetes.io/csi/xxx.csi.xxx.io^f2ee34c4-f297-49cb-8730-4442ceb1df4f podName: nodeName:}" failed. No retries permitted until 2022-11-25 10:20:45.402877857 +0800 CST m=+777.855686189 (durationBeforeRetry 500ms). Error: UnmountDevice failed for volume "pvc-1a4bcff1-f11d-456c-b91a-1aaa5c3ea5db" (UniqueName: "kubernetes.io/csi/xxx.csi.xxx.io^f2ee34c4-f297-49cb-8730-4442ceb1df4f") on node "192.168.3.181" : persistentvolumes "e6104b10fea107e004e3307b0444fd7b775fedd804ab47aa997118b7927c32e0" is forbidden: User "system:node:192.168.3.181" cannot get resource "persistentvolumes" in API group "" at the cluster scope: no relationship found between node '192.168.3.181' and this object
```
The global mount path is changed in the https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/107065. As a result, the `getDriverAndVolNameFromDeviceMountPath` method obtains incorrect pvName(e6104b10fea107e004e3307b0444fd7b775fedd804ab47aa997118b7927c32e0). 

**The unmountDevice operation may be performed multiple times in [1.19 - 1.25] kubernetes versions.** This problem does not occur before because `getDriverAndVolNameFromDeviceMountPath` can still obtain the correct pvName from the global mount path. However, this problem occurs after https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/107065 is merged.

### Q : Why is unmountDevice operation performed multiple times?
https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/29896262/204746895-2d7dd34b-9838-4f9d-8cba-02685037fcde.gif
### A : go routine scheduling mechanism

<br></br>

```go
func (c *csiAttacher) UnmountDevice(deviceMountPath string) error {
	if deviceMountPath == "" {
		klog.V(4).Info(log("attacher.UnmountDevice(%s) skip due to empty device mount path", deviceMountPath))
		return nil
	}

	klog.V(4).Info(log("attacher.UnmountDevice(%s)", deviceMountPath))
	// Setup
	var driverName, volID string
	dataDir := filepath.Dir(deviceMountPath)
	data, err := loadVolumeData(dataDir, volDataFileName)
	if err == nil {
		driverName = data[volDataKey.driverName]
		volID = data[volDataKey.volHandle]
	} else {
		klog.Error(log("UnmountDevice failed to load volume data file [%s]: %v", dataDir, err))

		// The volume might have been mounted by old CSI volume plugin. Fall back to the old behavior: read PV from API server
		driverName, volID, err = getDriverAndVolNameFromDeviceMountPath(c.k8s, deviceMountPath)
		if err != nil {
			klog.Errorf(log("attacher.UnmountDevice failed to get driver and volume name from device mount path: %v", err))
			return err
		}
	}
     ...
}
```
After the first unmountDevice operation is performed successfully, the vol_data.json file is deleted. So the subsequent unmountDevice operation will perform `getDriverAndVolNameFromDeviceMountPath` method because vol_data.json file doesn't exist.
